In <CCBL3E.HIs@ccu.umanitoba.ca> umcarman@ccu.umanitoba.ca (Chris D. Carman) writes:


>I am having problems with the colours on nh313386 for my MS DOS machine.
>The game runs perfectly, except that the colours are sometimes too dark.
>The offending colours are dark blue and gray.  It is very difficult to 
>pick out those dark blue fountains, and even more difficult to find the
>silly nymphs that sometimes come out of them.  Probably the most annoying
>thing about the inability to show dark blue the way it used to is that
>I keep walking into those darned dark blue floating eyes!

>Has anybody else experienced this?  I'm not sure how I can change the
>"dark blue" colour to a lighter one, so any help would be appreciated.

Try adding the following line to your NetHack.cnf file:

	videocolors = 4 2 6 9 5 3 12 10 14 9 13 11

Note that this will make dark blues appear the same as light blues, so 
it should only be done if you are experiencing a problem seeing the
darker blues.

